# Aranet4 -> InfluxDB collection, every 5 minutes, on officepi.
#
# Install:  crontab -e   (paste the line below)
# Verify:   crontab -l
#
# Changes from the original line:
#
#  * Calls the venv interpreter directly instead of
#    `/bin/bash -lc 'source ~/.bashrc && source sensors_env/bin/activate && ...'`.
#    Sourcing an interactive shell profile from cron was the cause of the
#    "failed cron runs" debugging in this repo's history -- cron has no
#    interactive shell, so ~/.bashrc's early non-interactive guard could skip
#    exactly the setup the job depended on. The venv's bin/python3 needs no
#    activation.
#
#  * stdout/stderr still land in cron.log, but the job no longer echoes its
#    INFO log there -- so cron.log now captures only real crashes instead of
#    duplicating aranet_logger.log byte for byte (they were 77 MB each).
#
# Health is reported to Prometheus through the node_exporter textfile collector
# (/var/lib/node_exporter/textfile_collector/aranet.prom), not by reading these
# logs. See observethis alert group `sensors_alerts`.

*/5 * * * * cd $HOME/repos/sensors && sensors_env/bin/python3 aranet_logger.py >> $HOME/repos/sensors/cron.log 2>&1

# ── Ecowitt GW1200B soil probes -> InfluxDB, every 5 minutes, on officepi ─────
#
# Offset by 2 minutes from the Aranet4 line above so the two jobs do not both
# wake a Raspberry Pi 3B at :00/:05/:10. They are independent; nothing breaks if
# they overlap, but staggering keeps the load flat and the logs readable.
#
# The gateway is polled over HTTP across the VLAN boundary to Arlo. It answers
# in ~70ms, so this run is far quicker than the Bluetooth one.

2-59/5 * * * * cd $HOME/repos/sensors && sensors_env/bin/python3 ecowitt_logger.py >> $HOME/repos/sensors/cron.log 2>&1
